## AbortController

```javascript
const controller = new AbortController();
fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal });
controller.abort();

// In an effect:
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  fetch(url, { signal: controller.signal })
    .then((r) => r.json())
    .then(setData)
    .catch((err) => { if (err.name !== 'AbortError') setError(err); });
  return () => controller.abort();
}, [url]);
```

**Why it matters:** without it, a slow request for `query="a"` can resolve *after* a fast one for `query="abc"` and overwrite the correct results. The abort makes the race impossible instead of unlikely.

## The Promise combinators

```javascript
await Promise.all([a, b, c]);        // all succeed, or reject on the FIRST failure
await Promise.allSettled([a, b, c]); // never rejects: [{status, value|reason}, ...]
await Promise.race([a, b]);          // first to SETTLE, success or failure
await Promise.any([a, b]);           // first to SUCCEED; rejects only if all fail
```

